@import owner.buriedoiltank.pages.FuelPageService.DeliveryPage
@import owner.buriedoiltank.heating.PriceArea
@param DeliveryPage page
@template.layout.page(meta = page.meta(), activeNav = "prices", content = @`
<header class="fuel-heading"><div class="v2-shell"><nav class="v2-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Heating oil delivery</span></nav><p class="v2-eyebrow">Selected suppliers · Direct quote routes</p><h1>Find heating oil delivery.<br>Compare the whole quote.</h1><p class="fuel-intro">Start with a supplier that lists your area, then confirm price, order minimum and timing directly. Six supplier websites cover selected areas in eight states.</p><p class="fuel-date">Source statements checked November 18, 2026. These are selected examples, not complete statewide coverage, partners or ranked recommendations.</p><nav class="fuel-jump"><a href="#suppliers">Find a supplier</a><a href="/heating-oil-prices/">Compare state benchmarks</a><a href="/heating-oil-cost-calculator/">Compare quote totals</a></nav></div></header>
<section class="v2-shell fuel-section" id="suppliers"><div class="fuel-section-head"><div><p class="v2-eyebrow">Supplier directory</p><h2>Check the actual delivery area.</h2></div><label>Filter by state<select data-supplier-state><option value="all">All listed states</option>@for (var id : PriceArea.PAGE_STATES.stream().filter(state -> owner.buriedoiltank.heating.HeatingOilSuppliers.ALL.stream().anyMatch(supplier -> supplier.states().contains(state))).toList())<option value="${id}">${PriceArea.require(id).name()}</option>@endfor</select></label></div><p data-supplier-count role="status">6 selected suppliers</p>
<div class="fuel-supplier-list">@for (var supplier : page.suppliers())<article data-supplier-states="${String.join(" ", supplier.states())}"><div><h3>${supplier.name()}</h3><p>${supplier.area()}</p></div><div><p>${supplier.terms()}</p><a href="${supplier.url()}" rel="external">Check coverage and current quote ↗</a></div></article>@endfor</div>
<p>No supplier listed for your town? The state filter is not an address match. Ask local suppliers whether they serve your address; do not assume a statewide price means statewide delivery.</p></section>
<section class="fuel-soft"><div class="v2-shell fuel-section fuel-two-column"><div><p class="v2-eyebrow">Before ordering</p><h2>Four things to confirm.</h2><ol><li>Fuel grade, actual address coverage and access to the fill.</li><li>Minimum order, any small-order fee and cash/card differences.</li><li>Total including applicable tax and fees.</li><li>Delivery date, inspection requirements and any restart service.</li></ol><a class="v2-button" href="/heating-oil-cost-calculator/">Compare two delivered totals ↗</a></div><div><h3>Know the gallons before you order.</h3><p>Use the correct model chart to estimate current gallons and available planning space. Your supplier confirms the authorized delivery amount.</p><p><a href="/oil-tank-gauge-calculator/">Read your tank ↗</a> · <a href="/how-much-heating-oil-do-i-need/">Plan order space ↗</a></p><h3>Already ran out?</h3><p>Ask the supplier about restart service and timing. A website's same-day claim does not guarantee a delivery slot.</p><a href="/ran-out-of-heating-oil/">No-heat and run-out guidance ↗</a></div></div></section>
<section class="v2-shell fuel-section fuel-source"><h2>Understand the order terms</h2><p><a href="/cash-heating-oil/">Cash/COD quotes</a> · <a href="/automatic-vs-will-call-heating-oil/">Automatic vs. will-call</a> · <a href="/heating-oil-minimum-delivery/">Minimum delivery quantities</a> · <a href="/heating-oil-guides/">All buying guides</a></p><h2>How these listings work</h2><p>Descriptions summarize the linked suppliers' own public pages as checked on November 18, 2026. Prices and availability can change; no orders, payment or personal details are collected here. Links go directly to suppliers and carry no referral tracking. We have not assessed service quality or independently verified licensing.</p><p>Compare a current quote with the <a href="/heating-oil-prices/">dated EIA benchmark</a>, or use the <a href="/heating-oil-delivery-check/">delivery-ticket cross-check</a> after a delivery.</p></section>
`)
